{
	"name": "Graverobber",
	"type": "background",
	"img": "icons/magic/death/grave-tombstone-glow-tan.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p><strong>Ability Score Increase:</strong> Constitution +1, any other attribute +1</p><p><strong>Skill Proficiencies:</strong> Deception, Stealth</p><p><strong>Tool Proficiencies:</strong> None</p><p><strong>Suggested Equipment (Cost 8 gold):</strong> Hemp rope 50ft, hooded lantern, shovel</p><p><em><strong>Feature:</strong></em><strong> Gravedigger.</strong> A job no one wishes to do, and few are willing to do: you’ve long become skilled at digging perfectly useable holes in the ground. With 3 hours of labor you can dig a grave instead of the usual 8. In communities with a cemetary, this affords you a moderate lifestyle for a day’s work, or a poor one in communities without as you are relegated to manual labor. In communities with necromancers or scientists looking for fresh cadavers, however, 3 hours of work secures a moderate lifestyle for a week. In addition, you can clear rubble in half the normal time.</p><p><em><strong>Adventures and Advancement:</strong></em> While there’s precious room for advancement in the digging of holes industry, if you’re willing to work for people who aren’t on the up and up, you can get yourself a rich lifestyle digging up bodies for a necromancer if you work 3 hours each day. The downside, of course, is that law enforcement and graveyard guardians become more and more severe as a resurrectionist plies their grisly trade.</p><p><strong>Connections and Memento:</strong> Roll 1d10, choose, or make up your own.</p><p>@Embed[Compendium.a5e.a5e-roll-tables.RollTable.MqeNLGhHF6ODMxdj caption=false cite=true rollable=true]</p><p>@Embed[Compendium.a5e.a5e-roll-tables.RollTable.wUKoD4mWPhCvSyKp caption=false cite=true rollable=true]</p>",
